      "location": "Statement",
      "defect": "missing-hypothesis",
      "evidence": "The item states without qualification: \"Every Bernstein set in R is not Lebesgue measurable.\" But its only cited supports are [L1] and [L2], whose source Statements both begin with the omitted hypothesis: thm-a-bernstein-set-has-inner-measure-zero-and-full-outer-measure-in-every-interval says \"Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice. Let B...\", and thm-bounded-subsets-of-r-are-lebesgue-measurable-exactly-when-inner-and-outer-measures-agree says \"Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice. Let E subseteq R be bounded.\" As written, the proof establishes only the countable-choice version, not the unconditional Statement.",
